upstream: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cloudflare/skills/main/skills/workers-best-practices
verified: 2026-11-22
scope: directory
reason: The current upstream entrypoint references the cf-cli sibling skill,
  which is not vendored in this dotfiles tree. Local points to its official
  upstream directory instead of creating a broken relative link or installing
  an unrelated skill. The rest of SKILL.md is byte-identical to the reviewed
  upstream entrypoint; existing reference files are preserved.
  2026-10-29: references/runtime-patterns.md "Be aware of platform limits" now
  states the current Free/Paid CPU limits; the retired Bundled/Standard/Unbound
  plan names were wrong against
  https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/. Drop this local
  change when upstream corrects the line.
would_lose_if_wired: A byte-for-byte refresh would reintroduce a reference to an
  unavailable local sibling and remove its reachable official source.
refresh_guard: _refresh-vendored.sh reports and preserves this managed fork.
  Compare upstream in a scratch directory, then retain the external pointer
  while the sibling is not intentionally adopted.
to_vendor: Restore the upstream sibling reference if cf-cli is deliberately
  installed as a canonical owned skill and its routing boundary is accepted.
recheck: 2026-11-22 — merged upstream 5108325 content changes since fe02920: (a) c9a7335 `@cloudflare/vitest-plugin` replaces
  `@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers` in references/runtime-patterns.md (heading, pitfall wording, link to the migration guide, and the
  `env` import from `cloudflare:workers`; checked against developers.cloudflare.com/workers/testing/vitest-integration: `env` and `exports`
  come from `cloudflare:workers`, `cloudflare:test` keeps the other helpers); (b) the new "Place Compute Near Regional Databases" section in
  SKILL.md and references/configuration.md plus the Hyperdrive note in runtime-patterns.md (region hint, Smart Placement only affects fetch
  handlers; checked against workers/configuration/placement). Local changes (cf-cli pointer, CPU limits wording) stand. skill-feedback: upstream added `references/skill-feedback.md` and a `## Skill feedback` pointer to every skill (cloudflare/skills 0e7a86d, 29de2b2). NOT adopted, on purpose: it instructs the agent to file a public GitHub issue on cloudflare/skills with `gh issue create`. Upstream itself gates it on showing the exact title and body and getting a yes, but a posting path from a shared, auto-loaded skill is an outbound action that belongs to the owner, and CORE's approval gates cover external publication. To adopt later: add the file and pointer per skill and keep the explicit-approval step.
description: 2026-10-30 skill-efficiency pass — frontmatter description rewritten to ≤250 chars (what + boundary front-loaded; Codex truncates at ~250). Body untouched by this pass. Re-apply after a byte-for-byte refresh; see docs/skill-efficiency-audit-2026-10-30.md.
